    "result_text": "The full suite passes (23 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year.\n\nThe project generates DTOs at build time via openapi-generator and maps them with MapStruct, and it already had a precedent for derived read-only fields (`initials`, `displayName`). I followed that same pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `readOnly` `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema (example `'SMI-0007-M26'`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a derived getter:\n   ```java\n   public String getMembershipNumber() {\n       if (this.customerCode == null || this.registrationDate == null) {\n           return null;\n       }\n       return String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", this.customerCode, this.registrationDate.getYear() % 100);\n   }\n   ```\n   MapStruct auto-maps `getMembershipNumber()` \u2192 `setMembershipNumber()` by name, so no mapper change was needed. The `%02d` handling ensures a year like 2005 yields `M05`. It's derived purely from the owner's own fields (matching the `Cp14Tests` \"seed-independent\" note), and safely returns `null` if either source field is absent.\n\nNo new field is persisted \u2014 it's computed on read, consistent with how `customerCode`/`registrationDate` feed it.",
